## 4. Method Reference & Usage Examples

### 1. `PlanHelper::filterEachPlan($plans = null, bool $hierarchical = false): Collection`
Filters all plans into their respective categories.
- **Default Flat Grouping (`$hierarchical = false`)**:
  ```php
  use App\Helpers\PlanHelper;

  $grouped = PlanHelper::filterEachPlan();

  // Access specific categories:
  $repoAccounts      = $grouped->get(PlanHelper::TYPE_FOR_REPOSSESSION);
  $ptpAccounts       = $grouped->get(PlanHelper::TYPE_PTP);
  $priority1Accounts = $grouped->get(PlanHelper::TYPE_PRIORITY_1);
  $nextActionPlans   = $grouped->get(PlanHelper::TYPE_NEXT_ACTION_PLAN);
  $fddNsAccounts     = $grouped->get(PlanHelper::TYPE_FDD_NS);
  $regularAccounts   = $grouped->get(PlanHelper::TYPE_REGULAR);
  ```

- **Hierarchical Grouping (`$hierarchical = true`)**:
  ```php
  $hierarchical = PlanHelper::filterEachPlan(null, true);

  $priorityAccounts = $hierarchical->get(PlanHelper::CATEGORY_PRIORITY);
  $regularAccounts  = $hierarchical->get(PlanHelper::CATEGORY_REGULAR);

  $repoInPriority = $priorityAccounts->get(PlanHelper::TYPE_FOR_REPOSSESSION);
  ```

### 2. `PlanHelper::filterPlansByType(Collection $plans, string $type): Collection`
Filters a collection of plans to return only those matching a given type or category name (also supports friendly aliases like `'ptp'`, `'repo'`, `'priority 1'`, `'regular'`).
```php
$repoPlans = PlanHelper::filterPlansByType($plans, PlanHelper::TYPE_FOR_REPOSSESSION);
$ptpPlans  = PlanHelper::filterPlansByType($plans, 'PTP');
$regPlans  = PlanHelper::filterPlansByType($plans, 'Regular Accounts');
```

### 3. Individual Classification Methods
- `PlanHelper::categorizePlan($plan)`: Returns detailed classification array (`main_category`, `subcategory`, `specific_type`, `matched_rules`).
- `PlanHelper::determineCategory($plan)`: Returns the subcategory string (e.g., `'For Repossession Accounts'`).
- `PlanHelper::determineMainCategory($plan)`: Returns `'Priority Accounts'` or `'Regular Accounts'`.

